{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b60f74ee8ad8602","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9018\n3\ttitle: GPU chargeback reporting for platform administrators\n4\tstatus: Refinement Done\n5\tpriority: Major\n6\tlabels:\n7\t- refined\n8\t- observability\n9\tlinks:\n10\t- 'depends-on: RHAISTRAT-9990 (GPU usage metering — in flight, separate strategy)'\n11\t---\n12\t\n13\t## Problem Statement\n14\t\n15\tPlatform teams fund shared GPU clusters but cannot attribute consumption to the\n16\tprojects using them, so capacity costs are socialized and heavy users have no\n17\tincentive to release resources. The in-flight metering strategy\n18\t(RHAISTRAT-9990) is delivering per-project GPU-hour usage data; this strategy\n19\tbuilds the administrator-facing chargeback reporting on top of that data. The\n20\tmetering data schema is owned by RHAISTRAT-9990 and is not final until that\n21\tstrategy lands — reporting work here consumes it, and must not re-implement\n22\tcollection.\n23\t\n24\t## High-Level Requirements\n25\t\n26\t| ID | Priority | Requirement |\n27\t|-------|----------|-------------|\n28\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges, computed from the metering data delivered by RHAISTRAT-9990. |\n29\t| HLR-2 | P1 | Reports can be exported as CSV and retrieved via a stable API for finance tooling. |\n30\t| HLR-3 | P1 | The Dashboard admin view shows current-month consumption against each project's Kueue quota. |\n31\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation covers report semantics (what counts as a GPU-hour) and export integration. |\n32\t\n33\t## Affected Components\n34\t\n35\t- Dashboard\n36\t- Distributed Workloads\n37\t\n38\t## Out of Scope\n39\t\n40\t- The metering collection pipeline itself (RHAISTRAT-9990)\n41\t- Currency/cost-rate modelling — reports are in GPU-hours, not dollars\n42\t\n43\t## Open Questions\n44\t\n45\t1. The metering data schema finalizes only when RHAISTRAT-9990 lands; report\n46\t   implementation consuming it carries that external timing risk.\n47\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b64fdb569a627dec","agent_id":"a4fb1e800e30ab2bc","session_id":"552a4708-ccc9-4336-802d-f1ef32ac46ea","uuid":"b4c954dc-f390-4ce7-a520-23fa376947bc","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:22:17.600Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b60f74ee8ad8602","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018 strategy"}
