view, export/API, quota comparison, and documentation epics exist and\ndeliver the same capability regardless of the schema's final field layout; the\nschema shapes field mapping inside those epics (an implementation detail the\nconsuming team resolves), and the timing is a schedule risk controlled by an\nexternal party. The unknown is therefore NOT a genuine unknown warranting an\nInvestigation epic. It is modeled as:\n\n- an **external precondition** recorded in the Risks/Notes of the consuming\n  epics (RHAISTRAT-9990 is a separate strategy — there is no epic in this\n  decomposition to draw a DAG edge to), and\n- **acceptance criteria on the consuming epics** phrased at the engineering\n  completion point they control (reports computed from the metering data as\n  delivered).\n\nThis also means no conditional branches: the outcome cannot add or remove epics\nin this plan.\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n|----|-------|------|------|-----------|----------|\n| RHAISTRAT-9018-E001 | Expose per-project Kueue quota data for chargeback reporting | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9018-E002 | Administrator GPU-hour consumption reports with CSV export and reporting API | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9018-E003 | Admin view of current-month consumption against Kueue quota | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9018-E004 | Document report semantics and export integration | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Docs | Documentation | P1 |\n\nEpic count: 4 (no branch epics).\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[RHAISTRAT-9018-E001 quota data exposure]\n    E002[RHAISTRAT-9018-E002 consumption reports + export/API]\n    E003[RHAISTRAT-9018-E003 consumption vs quota view]\n    E004[RHAISTRAT-9018-E004 documentation]\n    E001 --> E003\n    E002 --> E003\n    E001 --> E004\n    E002 --> E004\n    E003 --> E004\n```\n\nCritical path length: 3 (e.g., E002 → E003 → E004).\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E001 → E003 | Rule 13 (artifact consumed) | The quota comparison view builds against the per-project quota data surface E001 produces; the Dashboard owns no data plane and reads component-provided data. |\n| E002 → E003 | Rule 13 (shared surface) | HLR-3 renders the same per-project consumption data the reports epic surfaces; serializing avoids two Dashboard epics building the same consumption-reporting surface independently. |\n| E001 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation is blocked by every Implementation epic. |\n| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation is blocked by every Implementation epic. |\n| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation is blocked by every Implementation epic. |\n| (no edge) RHAISTRAT-9990 → E002/E003 | External precondition, not an edge | The metering strategy is a separate strategy outside this decomposition; its timing risk is recorded as a risk/AC on the consuming epics, never as a DAG edge to a nonexistent epic. |\n| (no edge) E001 ∥ E002 | Rule 14 (independent repos/artifacts) | Quota exposure (Kueue side) and consumption reporting (Dashboard, metering data) share no artifacts — they run in parallel. |\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Requirement (abridged) | Epic | Notes |\n|-----|----------|------------------------|------|-------|\n| HLR-1 | P0 | Per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges | RHAISTRAT-9018-E002 | Direct cover. |\n| HLR-2 | P1 | CSV export and stable API for finance tooling | RHAISTRAT-9018-E002 | **(bundled)** — CSV export and the retrieval API are presentation modes of the same per-project report surface and data access built for HLR-1; splitting would force a second epic to rebuild the same surface and data pipeline, so HLR-2 is not separately schedulable. Epic priority remains P0 from HLR-1. |\n| HLR-3 | P1 | Dashboard admin view shows current-month consumption against Kueue quota | RHAISTRAT-9018-E003 | Split from E002 (not bundled): the quota comparison is a distinct, deferrable feature that additionally depends on the Distributed Workloads quota data exposure — bundling it into the P0 reports epic would serialize P0 reporting behind Distributed Workloads quota work. E003 consumes the reporting surface built by E002 (E002 → E003 edge) so the surface is not duplicated. The quota-data half of HLR-3 is enabled by RHAISTRAT-9018-E001. |\n| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation covers report semantics and export integration | RHAISTRAT-9018-E004 | docs-authoring epic; priority P1 per the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy frontmatter priority Major → P1), not inherited from HLR-4's P2. |\n\nAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements. No redundant/overlapping\nHLR pairs were found (HLR-1 and HLR-3 are distinct views — time-range reports\nvs current-month quota comparison — over related but differently-sourced data).\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n1. **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): no Impacted Teams table, no\n   Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, no NFRs. Teams\n   were inferred from architecture context; epic ACs were derived from HLRs.\n   The refinement record for this strategy should be asked to supply ACs and\n   NFRs before implementation sign-off.\n2. **External timing risk (scope trap)**: E002 and E003 consume the metering\n   data schema owned by RHAISTRAT-9990, which is not final until that strategy\n   lands. This is an externally controlled schedule constraint — recorded as a\n   risk on both epics with ACs written at the engineering completion point the\n   epics control; it cannot be compressed by this decomposition. If\n   RHAISTRAT-9990's final schema cannot support per-project attribution over\n   time ranges, E002/E003 require rework (rewrite), and HLR-4's semantics\n   section changes accordingly.\n3. **Ambiguous API placement**: the strategy does not state where the \"stable\n   API for finance tooling\" (HLR-2) lives. Dashboard architecture context says\n   the Dashboard owns no data plane and its interfaces are the Kubernetes API;\n   a finance-facing reporting API is therefore an assumption — it is placed\n   with the Dashboard reporting epic (the reporting surface this strategy\n   builds). If review locates the API in a backend component instead, E002\n   splits into a Dashboard view epic plus a backend API epic.\n4. **Affected Components listed without change descriptions**: the strategy\n   lists components only. The quota-data exposure epic for Distributed\n   Workloads is inferred from HLR-3's \"against each project's Kueue quota\" —\n   Kueue quota is owned by Distributed Workloads per architecture context.\n5. **Docs priority vs HLR priority**: E004 is P1 (docs-authoring exception,\n   strategy priority Major) while its only HLR (HLR-4) is P2 — expected per\n   the docs-authoring priority exception, noted here for reviewers.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nThe external dependency (RHAISTRAT-9990 metering data, uncertain timing) was\nevaluated for tiered delivery. Partial value IS deliverable without it:\n\n- **Tier 1 (independent of the metering strategy)**:\n  RHAISTRAT-9018-E001 — per-project Kueue quota data exposure. Built entirely\n  on Kueue data available today; de-risks the quota-comparison integration and\n  can start immediately.\n- **Tier 2 (gated on the external metering strategy delivering its final\n  schema)**: RHAISTRAT-9018-E002 and RHAISTRAT-9018-E003 — all\n  consumption-dependent reporting work. The gate is an external precondition\n  (risk + AC on each epic), not a DAG edge. RHAISTRAT-9018-E004 (docs)\n  follows all implementations per Rule 11.\n\nComponent mapping notes: all epic `component` values (Dashboard, Distributed\nWorkloads, Documentation) are verbatim canonical names from\n`.context/rhai-components.txt`; no non-obvious mappings were needed.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":38641,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b64fdb569a627dec","agent_id":"a4fb1e800e30ab2bc","session_id":"552a4708-ccc9-4336-802d-f1ef32ac46ea","uuid":"b9b93345-f550-4d73-99f2-01ba1d999c60","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:26:56.532Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018 strategy"}
