{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-aa3cd979-51bd-4770-9453-642d0ee5d74f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d2b4de39a0fb0a1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-jg7mt6ku/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E001.md","content":"# Expose per-project Kueue quota data for chargeback reporting\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers a per-project Kueue quota data surface that administrator\nchargeback reporting can consume. Platform administrators need to see GPU\nconsumption against each project's Kueue quota; Kueue (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue\nquota model) is owned by the Distributed Workloads component, and the Dashboard\n— which renders the admin views — owns no data plane and reads\ncomponent-provided data. This epic makes each project's quota figure\nretrievable for reporting, building on Kueue's existing quota model and\nmetrics exposure. It involves no metering collection: per-project GPU-hour\nusage data is delivered by the separate in-flight metering strategy and is out\nof scope here.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Expose per-project Kueue quota figures (derived from the\n  ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model) in a form the administrator reporting\n  views can consume for the current-month window they require.\n- Cover every project that holds a Kueue quota; projects without quota are\n  reported as such rather than omitted silently.\n- Build on the existing Kueue quota model and metrics interfaces; the exposure\n  mechanism (metrics extension, API, or aggregated CR reading) is an\n  implementation decision for the owning team.\n- Out of scope: any metering/usage collection (owned by the separate metering\n  strategy), and any Dashboard-side rendering (owned by the Dashboard team).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a project with a configured Kueue quota, the quota figure surfaced for\n  that project matches the configured quota — measured by comparing the\n  exposed figure against the ClusterQueue/LocalQueue configuration for a\n  sample of projects with differing quota values.\n- Every project holding a Kueue quota is retrievable; projects without quota\n  are distinguishable from quota-holding projects — measured by enumerating\n  projects and verifying none with quota is missing from the exposure.\n- The quota data is queryable for current-month reporting at the granularity\n  the admin view requires — measured by a successful retrieval covering all\n  quota-holding projects in a test cluster.\n- No changes are made to metering/usage collection — measured by the metering\n  pipeline's configuration and code remaining untouched by this epic's\n  changes.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P1, partial — enabling)**: \"The Dashboard admin view shows\n  current-month consumption against each project's Kueue quota\" — this epic\n  delivers the quota-data half of HLR-3 (the Kueue quota side); the\n  admin-view rendering is delivered by the Dashboard epic that consumes this\n  data.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":43916,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b64fdb569a627dec","agent_id":"a4fb1e800e30ab2bc","session_id":"552a4708-ccc9-4336-802d-f1ef32ac46ea","uuid":"92a3f134-fe25-4c73-a512-aad67764755c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:27:09.476Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018 strategy"}
