{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-2371debb-2899-4350-aa3f-a75ebdaf43f0","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-969053e32145bb8e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-jg7mt6ku/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E002.md","content":"# Administrator GPU-hour consumption reports with CSV export and reporting API\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the core administrator-facing chargeback reporting\ncapability: per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time\nranges, computed from the metering data delivered by the separate in-flight\nmetering strategy, rendered in the Dashboard's administrator view. It also\ndelivers export of those reports as CSV and retrieval via a stable API for\nfinance tooling. This epic consumes the metering data — it must not\nre-implement collection, which is owned by the metering strategy.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Administrator report view in the Dashboard listing per-project GPU-hour\n  consumption for a selectable time range, computed from the delivered\n  metering data.\n- CSV export of the report for the selected time range.\n- A stable retrieval API over the same report data, suitable for finance\n  tooling integration, with a documented contract.\n- Reading and aggregating the metering data as delivered by the metering\n  strategy (the per-project GPU-hour usage data source); no collection\n  pipeline logic.\n- Out of scope: currency/cost-rate modelling (reports are in GPU-hours, not\n  dollars), the metering collection pipeline itself, and Kueue quota\n  comparison (delivered by the quota-comparison view built on this reporting\n  surface).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given metered per-project GPU-hour usage, an administrator can generate a\n  report for any selectable time range listing per-project GPU-hour\n  consumption — measured by comparing report totals per project against the\n  metering source totals for the same range and projects.\n- The report can be exported as CSV — measured by the CSV contents matching\n  the on-screen report for the same time range and project set.\n- The report data is retrievable via a stable API with a documented contract\n  — measured by a finance-tooling-style client retrieving a report for a time\n  range through the API and receiving the same figures as the view.\n- Report computation consumes the metering data as delivered by the metering\n  strategy — measured by the epic introducing no usage-collection logic (the\n  metering pipeline remains the sole collector).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)**: \"Administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption\n  reports over selectable time ranges, computed from the metering data\n  delivered by\" the metering strategy — direct cover.\n- **HLR-2 (P1, bundled)**: \"Reports can be exported as CSV and retrieved via\n  a stable API for finance tooling\" — bundled into this epic rather than\n  split: CSV export and the retrieval API are presentation modes of the same\n  per-project report surface and data access built for HLR-1, so a separate\n  epic would rebuild the same surface and is not separately schedulable. Epic\n  priority remains P0 from HLR-1.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- **External timing risk**: the metering data schema is owned by the in-flight\n  metering strategy and finalizes only when that strategy lands. Field\n  mapping and GPU-hour semantics may shift until then; this epic's\n  implementation consumes the schema as delivered. This schedule constraint\n  is externally controlled and cannot be compressed here — if the final\n  schema cannot support per-project attribution over time ranges, this epic's\n  computation layer requires rework.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44666,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b64fdb569a627dec","age