jects.\n- Projects without quota are visibly distinguishable from quota-holding\n  projects — measured by a project with consumption but no quota appearing\n  with an explicit no-quota indication rather than being omitted.\n- The view consumes the existing per-project consumption reporting surface\n  rather than re-implementing consumption data access — measured by the epic\n  introducing no independent metering-data query path.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P1)**: \"The Dashboard admin view shows current-month consumption\n  against each project's Kueue quota\" — direct cover (quota-data side enabled\n  by the Distributed Workloads quota exposure; rendering delivered here).\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- **External timing risk**: consumption figures derive from the metering data\n  delivered by the in-flight metering strategy, whose schema finalizes only\n  when that strategy lands — externally controlled timing that cannot be\n  compressed here; consumption semantics may shift until then.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45563,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b64fdb569a627dec","agent_id":"a4fb1e800e30ab2bc","session_id":"552a4708-ccc9-4336-802d-f1ef32ac46ea","uuid":"5c8ba1f4-b44a-4cef-a8db-4d7fdf708d74","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:27:32.059Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018 strategy"}
