{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8a0684b6af40cba","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9018\n3\tscore: 14\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: minor\n8\t  criterion: AI Implementability Scoring\n9\t  description: E003 existing_foundation rationale cites two landed surfaces that are\n10\t    actually in-decomposition epics (E001/E002), not pre-existing foundation; re-word\n11\t    the rationale to cite the existing GA Dashboard console that the epic extends\n12\t- severity: minor\n13\t  criterion: Completeness\n14\t  description: E002 Risks/Notes carries the metering timing risk but not the API-placement\n15\t    ambiguity (Health Warning 3 in the summary); record the placement assumption and\n16\t    its conditional split trigger in E002 Risks/Notes\n17\terror: null\n18\t---\n19\t## Review Summary\n20\t\n21\tScore: 14/14 — pass\n22\tRecommendation: accept\n23\t\n24\tContract validator: OK (`validate_decomposition.py` exited 0 — epic body\n25\tsections, canonical component names, Rule 11 docs-last coverage, priority\n26\tinheritance, implementation-type parallelism, and shared-surface enforcement\n27\tall pass). Triage consistency: `triage: null` (full decomposition), epic_count\n28\t4 — consistent. No conditional branch files exist, matching the summary's\n29\t\"no branch epics\" statement.\n30\t\n31\tThe decomposition is a clean, well-justified translation of the strategy.\n32\tEvery HLR maps to at least one epic with a traceability matrix present; the\n33\tDAG is acyclic, matches the frontmatter `dependencies` exactly (arrow\n34\tdirection dependency → dependent), and every edge is justified (Rule 13\n35\tartifact/shared-surface edges into E003, Rule 11 docs-last edges into E004);\n36\tE001 and E002 correctly run in parallel. The single open question (metering\n37\tschema timing) is correctly modeled as an external precondition (risk + ACs\n38\tat the engineering completion point) rather than an Investigation epic — its\n39\toutcome cannot add or remove epics. Two minor, non-blocking observations are\n40\trecorded below.\n41\t\n42\t## Criterion Details\n43\t\n44\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n45\tAll four HLRs covered: HLR-1 → E002 (direct), HLR-2 → E002 (bundled, with a\n46\t`(bundled)` flag and self-contained rationale in the matrix row — CSV export\n47\tand the retrieval API are presentation modes of the one report surface, so\n48\tbundling is the correct shape), HLR-3 → E001 (quota-data half, enabling) +\n49\tE003 (rendering), HLR-4 → E004. Traceability matrix present and complete.\n50\tPriority inheritance is sound: E001 (P1) blocks only P1 work (E003) and the\n51\tdocs epic (exempt); no lower-priority epic blocks P0 work (E002 has no\n52\tdependencies). No priority collapse with deferrable features — HLR-3 is\n53\tcorrectly split out as a deferrable P1 feature rather than collapsed into the\n54\tP0 reports epic (which would have serialized P0 reporting behind E001 or\n55\tbundled cross-team work); HLR-2's bundling into E002 is justified same-surface\n56\tbundling, recorded in the matrix row. E004's P1 (docs-authoring exception,\n57\tstrategy priority Major → P1) is correctly derived, not inherited from HLR-4's\n58\tP2.\n59\t\n60\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n61\tNo circular dependencies; no invalid edges (all referenced epics exist); no\n62\tbranch epics referenced by main-plan epics. Diagram/frontmatter cross-check\n63\tpasses exactly: diagram edges E001→E003, E002→E003, E001→E004, E002→E004,\n64\tE003→E004 match E003's `dependencies: [E001, E002]` and E004's\n65\t`dependencies: [E001, E002, E003]`; E001 and E002 have empty `dependencies`,\n66\tmatching the declared E001 ∥ E002 parallelism (Rule 14 — different components,\n67\tno shared artifacts). Arrow direction is dependency → dependent as required.\n68\tEdges are justified: E001→E003 and E002→E003 are Rule 13 artifact/shared-\n69\tsurface dependencies discoverable from E003's scope (it consumes both the\n70\tquota exposure and the reporting surface); the three edges into E004 are Rule\n71\t11 docs-last. No konflux/license/repo-onboarding epics exist, so Rules 7/8/10\n72\tparallelism is not applicable (both components are documented as already\n73\tKonflux-onboarded). Cross-check for missing edges: the metering-data\n74\tdependency is external to this decomposition (RHAISTRAT-9990 has no epic\n75\there) and is correctly carried as a risk/AC rather than a DAG edge. Critical\n76\tpath length 3 is reasonable for a strategy of this size (M standard: 3-4).\n77\t\n78\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n79\tComponent/team tuples produce separate epics: E001 (Distributed Workloads /\n80\tDistributed Workloads), E002 and E003 (Dashboard / RHOAI Dashboard), E004\n81\t(Documentation / RHOAI Docs) — all canonical component names verified against\n82\t`.context/rhai-components.txt`. No epic spans multiple components or teams.\n83\tNo work-product type mixing: E004 is a standalone docs-authoring epic and the\n84\tcode epics contain no content authoring. No standalone enforcement-tool epic.\n85\tNo scope duplication: the E002/E003 split is not a same-surface presentation\n86\tsplit — E003 is a distinct, deferrable feature (quota comparison) that\n87\tadditionally depends on E001's cross-component quota-data exposure; merging it\n88\tinto P0 E002 would create a priority-inheritance violation or a cross-team\n89\tepic, and the decomposition records this reasoning in the HLR-3 matrix row.\n90\tE003's scope explicitly consumes (not rebuilds) E002's reporting surface, so\n91\tneither epic duplicates the other's work. Sizes are within the ~2-week\n92\tguideline; E002 (report view + CSV + API over one surface) is a single logical\n93\tchange, not a heterogeneous monolith.\n94\t\n95\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n96\tAll four epics are Implementation and each produces a concrete artifact (quota\n97\tdata surface, report view + CSV + API, quota-comparison view, published\n98\tdocumentation); E004 correctly carries `implementation_type: docs-authoring`.\n99\tThe absence of an Investigation epic is correctly justified: the strategy's\n100\tsingle open question (metering schema finalization timing) does not change\n101\twhich downstream epics exist or what they do — it shapes field mapping inside\n102\tE002/E003 and is an externally controlled schedule risk, so it is correctly\n103\tmodeled as a precondition (risk + ACs), not a gate. No `gated_by` fields are\n104\tset anywhere, so there are no gate-metadata errors (no `gated_by` without\n105\t`gate_failure_impact`, no Investigation dependency without `gated_by`, no\n106\tnon-direct `gated_by` targets).\n107\t\n108\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n109\tAll epics are Implementation type and carry `ai_signals` (the 9-signal rubric)\n110\twith `investigation_signals: null` — correct signal-set pairing. All four\n111\tai-signals rationale files exist and their values match the frontmatter\n112\texactly. Signal values are consistent with the strategy and the rubric:\n113\tE002/E003's `open_questions: -1` and `external_dependency: -1` are justified\n114\tby the unsettled metering schema and the cross-strategy dependency;\n115\tE001's `open_questions: 0` / `external_dependency: 1` are correct (quota\n116\texposure touches neither). `architecture_claims` calibration verified against\n117\t`.context`: E001/E002/E003 score 1 with citations to the covering\n118\t`distributed-workloads.md` / `dashboard.md` files (both exist and corroborate\n119\tthe cited claims — Kueue ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model, Prometheus\n120\tmetrics, Dashboard owns no data plane); E004 scores 0 with the correct\n121\trationale that no architecture-context file covers the Documentation\n122\tcomponent. Arithmetic/thresholds not checked (pipeline-computed). One wording\n123\tnit (minor, non-docking): E003's `existing_foundation` rationale describes\n124\t\"two landed surfaces\" that are a