{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-82e96065215f8f3d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E002\n3\ttitle: Administrator GPU-hour consumption reports with CSV export and reporting API\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: -1\n16\t  external_dependency: -1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 3\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Administrator GPU-hour consumption reports with CSV export and reporting API\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the core administrator-facing chargeback reporting\n34\tcapability: per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time\n35\tranges, computed from the metering data delivered by the separate in-flight\n36\tmetering strategy, rendered in the Dashboard's administrator view. It also\n37\tdelivers export of those reports as CSV and retrieval via a stable API for\n38\tfinance tooling. This epic consumes the metering data — it must not\n39\tre-implement collection, which is owned by the metering strategy.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Administrator report view in the Dashboard listing per-project GPU-hour\n44\t  consumption for a selectable time range, computed from the delivered\n45\t  metering data.\n46\t- CSV export of the report for the selected time range.\n47\t- A stable retrieval API over the same report data, suitable for finance\n48\t  tooling integration, with a documented contract.\n49\t- Reading and aggregating the metering data as delivered by the metering\n50\t  strategy (the per-project GPU-hour usage data source); no collection\n51\t  pipeline logic.\n52\t- Out of scope: currency/cost-rate modelling (reports are in GPU-hours, not\n53\t  dollars), the metering collection pipeline itself, and Kueue quota\n54\t  comparison (delivered by the quota-comparison view built on this reporting\n55\t  surface).\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Given metered per-project GPU-hour usage, an administrator can generate a\n60\t  report for any selectable time range listing per-project GPU-hour\n61\t  consumption — measured by comparing report totals per project against the\n62\t  metering source totals for the same range and projects.\n63\t- The report can be exported as CSV — measured by the CSV contents matching\n64\t  the on-screen report for the same time range and project set.\n65\t- The report data is retrievable via a stable API with a documented contract\n66\t  — measured by a finance-tooling-style client retrieving a report for a time\n67\t  range through the API and receiving the same figures as the view.\n68\t- Report computation consumes the metering data as delivered by the metering\n69\t  strategy — measured by the epic introducing no usage-collection logic (the\n70\t  metering pipeline remains the sole collector).\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: \"Administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption\n75\t  reports over selectable time ranges, computed from the metering data\n76\t  delivered by\" the metering strategy — direct cover.\n77\t- **HLR-2 (P1, bundled)**: \"Reports can be exported as CSV and retrieved via\n78\t  a stable API for finance tooling\" — bundled into this epic rather than\n79\t  split: CSV export and the retrieval API are presentation modes of the same\n80\t  per-project report surface and data access built for HLR-1, so a separate\n81\t  epic would rebuild the same surface and is not separately schedulable. Epic\n82\t  priority remains P0 from HLR-1.\n83\t\n84\t## Risks / Notes\n85\t\n86\t- **External timing risk**: the metering data schema is owned by the in-flight\n87\t  metering strategy and finalizes only when that strategy lands. Field\n88\t  mapping and GPU-hour semantics may shift until then; this epic's\n89\t  implementation consumes the schema as delivered. This schedule constraint\n90\t  is externally controlled and cannot be compressed here — if the final\n91\t  schema cannot support per-project attribution over time ranges, this epic's\n92\t  computation layer requires rework.\n93\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b01208ee235899a7","agent_id":"ae699aec38cbf1909","session_id":"552a4708-ccc9-4336-802d-f1ef32ac46ea","uuid":"6fb8f067-ad49-46f5-8ae2-8fc930902d7f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:32:55.293Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-82e96065215f8f3d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
