{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b143595dfa90a09f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n3\ttitle: Expose per-project Kueue quota data for chargeback reporting\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Expose per-project Kueue quota data for chargeback reporting\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers a per-project Kueue quota data surface that administrator\n34\tchargeback reporting can consume. Platform administrators need to see GPU\n35\tconsumption against each project's Kueue quota; Kueue (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue\n36\tquota model) is owned by the Distributed Workloads component, and the Dashboard\n37\t— which renders the admin views — owns no data plane and reads\n38\tcomponent-provided data. This epic makes each project's quota figure\n39\tretrievable for reporting, building on Kueue's existing quota model and\n40\tmetrics exposure. It involves no metering collection: per-project GPU-hour\n41\tusage data is delivered by the separate in-flight metering strategy and is out\n42\tof scope here.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Expose per-project Kueue quota figures (derived from the\n47\t  ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model) in a form the administrator reporting\n48\t  views can consume for the current-month window they require.\n49\t- Cover every project that holds a Kueue quota; projects without quota are\n50\t  reported as such rather than omitted silently.\n51\t- Build on the existing Kueue quota model and metrics interfaces; the exposure\n52\t  mechanism (metrics extension, API, or aggregated CR reading) is an\n53\t  implementation decision for the owning team.\n54\t- Out of scope: any metering/usage collection (owned by the separate metering\n55\t  strategy), and any Dashboard-side rendering (owned by the Dashboard team).\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Given a project with a configured Kueue quota, the quota figure surfaced for\n60\t  that project matches the configured quota — measured by comparing the\n61\t  exposed figure against the ClusterQueue/LocalQueue configuration for a\n62\t  sample of projects with differing quota values.\n63\t- Every project holding a Kueue quota is retrievable; projects without quota\n64\t  are distinguishable from quota-holding projects — measured by enumerating\n65\t  projects and verifying none with quota is missing from the exposure.\n66\t- The quota data is queryable for current-month reporting at the granularity\n67\t  the admin view requires — measured by a successful retrieval covering all\n68\t  quota-holding projects in a test cluster.\n69\t- No changes are made to metering/usage collection — measured by the metering\n70\t  pipeline's configuration and code remaining untouched by this epic's\n71\t  changes.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- **HLR-3 (P1, partial — enabling)**: \"The Dashboard admin view shows\n76\t  current-month consumption against each project's Kueue quota\" — this epic\n77\t  delivers the quota-data half of HLR-3 (the Kueue quota side); the\n78\t  admin-view rendering is delivered by the Dashboard epic that consumes this\n79\t  data.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d0ce63d890ed8ff","agent_id":"af6c6123c853fe289","session_id":"552a4708-ccc9-4336-802d-f1ef32ac46ea","uuid":"3cb4ae5d-27a3-44f3-9bb1-db6a8636106c",