{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99a05909ed7b7e32","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E003\n3\ttitle: Admin view of current-month consumption against Kueue quota\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E002\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 0\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: -1\n18\t  external_dependency: -1\n19\t  human_process_gates: 1\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 3\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Admin view of current-month consumption against Kueue quota\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic delivers the Dashboard administrator view showing each project's\n36\tcurrent-month GPU-hour consumption against its Kueue quota. It builds on two\n37\texisting surfaces: the per-project consumption reporting surface delivered by\n38\tthe administrator reports capability (which this epic extends rather than\n39\tduplicates) and the per-project Kueue quota data exposure delivered by the\n40\tDistributed Workloads component.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Current-month view in the Dashboard admin surface showing, per project,\n45\t  GPU-hour consumption alongside that project's Kueue quota.\n46\t- Consumption figures sourced from the same per-project metering-data\n47\t  reporting surface used by the consumption reports (no separate consumption\n48\t  data access is built).\n49\t- Quota figures sourced from the per-project Kueue quota data exposure.\n50\t- Projects without a Kueue quota are presented distinctly (consumption shown,\n51\t  quota marked absent) rather than dropped from the view.\n52\t- Out of scope: metering collection, quota data exposure itself, CSV/API\n53\t  export, and currency/cost-rate modelling.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- Given the current calendar month, the admin view shows each project's\n58\t  consumption against its Kueue quota — measured by comparing displayed\n59\t  figures against the metering-source consumption totals and the configured\n60\t  Kueue quotas for a sample of projects.\n61\t- Quota figures displayed match the configured Kueue quotas — measured by\n62\t  reconciling the view's quota column against ClusterQueue/LocalQueue\n63\t  configuration for quota-holding projects.\n64\t- Projects without quota are visibly distinguishable from quota-holding\n65\t  projects — measured by a project with consumption but no quota appearing\n66\t  with an explicit no-quota indication rather than being omitted.\n67\t- The view consumes the existing per-project consumption reporting surface\n68\t  rather than re-implementing consumption data access — measured by the epic\n69\t  introducing no independent metering-data query path.\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: \"The Dashboard admin view shows current-month consumption\n74\t  against each project's Kueue quota\" — direct cover (quota-data side enabled\n75\t  by the Distributed Workloads quota exposure; rendering delivered here).\n76\t\n77\t## Risks / Notes\n78\t\n79\t- **External timing risk**: consumption figures derive from the metering data\n80\t  delivered by the in-flight metering strategy, whose schema finalizes only\n81\t  when that strategy lands — externally controlled timing that cannot be\n82\t  compressed here; consumption semantics may shift until then.\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d0ce63d890ed8ff","agent_id":"af6c6123c853fe289","session_id":"552a4708-ccc9-4336-802d-f1ef32ac46ea","uuid":"307d4e0a-7ffa-4fd9-99da-00307bb7ec89","timestamp":"2026-10-2